        for (int num : nums) {
            if (largest == null || num > largest) {
                secondLargest = largest;
                largest = num;
            } else if (num < largest &&
                       (secondLargest == null || num > secondLargest)) {
                secondLargest = num;
            }
        }

        if (secondLargest == null) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException(
                "Array must contain at least two distinct values"
            );
        }

        return secondLargest;
    }
}
```

This returns the second-largest **distinct** value. For an empty array, null input, or an array whose elements are all equal, no valid second-largest value exists, so it throws `IllegalArgumentException`.

